From: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: give the RX rings room for a 10G burst

Most RX rings hold only 32 descriptors.  At 10G a 1 KiB
packet consumes a slot roughly every 800 ns, so 32 slots buy about 25 us
of slack - less than one NAPI poll takes when the ring is drained with a
full budget.  The QDMA then runs dry and starts dropping.

Ring 0 is the CPU port and already had 1024 descriptors.  The four rings
that carry the multi-gigabit ports (2, 4, 11, 15) are raised to 256 and
the rest to 128.  At 32 bytes per descriptor and 1 KiB buffers that is
~172 KiB of descriptors and ~5 MiB of buffers, which a 2 GiB board takes
without noticing.

This does not change the memory window reserved for hardware forwarding
(qdma0/qdma1-buf): those are separate regions sized by the DTS.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
---

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -39,12 +39,29 @@
 #define HW_DSCP_NUM			2048
 #define IRQ_QUEUE_LEN(_n)		((_n) ? 1024 : 2048)
 #define TX_DSCP_NUM			1024
+/* A ring that has 32 slots leaves the QDMA only a few microseconds of slack
+ * before it starts dropping: at 10G a 1 KB packet consumes a slot roughly
+ * every 800 ns, and NAPI only refills the ring after it has drained a whole
+ * budget. The 32-entry default was sized for the gigabit reference board,
+ * not for a port running at 10G.
+ *
+ * Ring 0 is the CPU port and keeps its 1024. The four rings that carry the
+ * multi-gigabit ports get 256, everything else 128. At 32 bytes per
+ * descriptor that is ~190 KiB of descriptors in total, plus the matching
+ * page_pool buffers, which a 2 GiB board absorbs without trouble.
+ *
+ * All 32 rings are initialised (RX_DONE_INT_MASK is 0xffffffff, so
+ * airoha_qdma_init_rx() skips none of them), but the four bank masks in
+ * RX_IRQ_BANK_PIN_MASK() between them name only 25 ring numbers.  The
+ * sizes below therefore only have to be sane for rings that can actually
+ * raise an interrupt; the remaining ones are sized like the rest.
+ */
 #define RX_DSCP_NUM(_n)			\
-	((_n) ==  2 ? 128 :		\
-	 (_n) ==  4 ? 128 :		\
-	 (_n) == 11 ? 128 :		\
-	 (_n) == 15 ? 128 :		\
-	 (_n) ==  0 ? 1024 : 32)
+	((_n) ==  2 ? 256 :		\
+	 (_n) ==  4 ? 256 :		\
+	 (_n) == 11 ? 256 :		\
+	 (_n) == 15 ? 256 :		\
+	 (_n) ==  0 ? 1024 : 128)
 
 #define AIROHA_LRO_PAGE_ORDER		get_order(SZ_16K)
 #define AIROHA_MAX_NUM_LRO_QUEUES	8
